# Keep the build context small and free of anything that should not enter an image layer.
#
# Two independent reasons, not just speed:
#   * ``data/`` and ``artifacts/`` hold the corpus, the trained checkpoints and the descriptor cache,
#     which is gigabytes. They are mounted at run time instead, so baking them in would make the
#     image enormous and couple model updates to code releases.
#   * ``.git/`` carries the full history, and ``.kaggle/`` and any ``.env`` would carry credentials.
#     A layer is forever, so the exclusion has to happen here rather than downstream.

# version control and credentials
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.kaggle
.env
.env.*

# corpora, checkpoints, caches, generated reports
data/
artifacts/
outputs/
runs/
pretrained_models/
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.onnx
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz

# local environments and tooling state
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# documentation and editor state: the runtime image does not read them, and docs/archive holds
# third-party material that must not be redistributed inside an image.
docs/archive/
*.md
!README.md
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
